{"id": "20496353", "revid": "35936988", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20496353", "title": "Nirlirnaqtuuq", "text": "Nirlirnaqtuuq (\"\u14c2\u1550\u14d5\u1550\u14c7\u1585\u1451\u1585\" formerly Neerlonakto Island (alternate: Nerdlernartoq,) is an irregularly shaped, extremely flat, uninhabited island in the Qikiqtaaluk Region, Nunavut, Canada. It is located in Foxe Basin with the mainland's Melville Peninsula is to the west and Baffin Island is to the north. The Inuit community of Igloolik is located southwest, on Igloo Island. Tern Island is to the east."}
