{"id": "20498655", "revid": "35936988", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20498655", "title": "Saint Paul's Vestry House", "text": "The Saint Paul's Vestry House is a historic building in Lynchburg, Virginia, United States. It was built about 1855 and is a single-story Classical Revival-style building with a simple low pitched gable roof and a rectangular plan. It is likely the only vestry house built exclusively for the governing body of an Episcopal Church in Virginia. It also served as the first home of the Lynchburg Woman's Club from 1903 to 1916.\nIt was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1997."}
