{"id": "20499160", "revid": "1951353", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20499160", "title": "Brian Oliver (triple jumper)", "text": "Brian Thomas Oliver (26 September 1929 \u2013 20 October 2015) was an Australian Olympic athlete who specialised in the triple jump, long jump and sprint running. He won the triple jump event at the 1950 British Empire Games and placed 23rd at the 1956 Summer Olympics. Oliver won the national triple jump title in 1953\u201354 and 1956, and the long jump title in 1953 and 1956. He was ranked #3 in the world in 1950 and #4 in 1953 in the triple jump."}
